SiliconForest
=============

SiliconForest is a fork of PureDarwin for Apple Silicon Macs (first target: the 13-inch M1
MacBook Pro, J293). It is built from the work of many other projects. This file names them,
with the licence each declares and what SiliconForest takes from it.

The licences are as the sources declare them; this file is a provenance record, not a legal
review. Every file taken from another project keeps its own copyright and licence notice, and
the SiliconForest rename never changes such a line (docs/design/siliconforest-naming.md).
The code written for SiliconForest itself is under the MIT License (LICENSE, "Copyright (c)
2026 Chris Kearney and the SiliconForest contributors"). That licence covers nothing else:
files ported from GPL sources are GPL as marked in each file, and every adopted file keeps
the licence it came with.

How to read the licence statements below. "Read from" names the licence file the statement
was read from (in this repository, or in the local clone the build uses). "Not verified"
means the statement comes from the project's public description or from package metadata
and no licence file was read for it here; it is to be checked before a release.

The per-directory NOTICE files are more exact than this file and take precedence for their
directory: integrations/siliconforest/m1-apcie-bridge/NOTICE (and NOTICE-bringup,
NOTICE-linkup), m1-apcie-host/NOTICE, m1-atcphy/NOTICE, m1-avd/NOTICE, m1-ave/NOTICE (and
m1-ave/tools/upstream/NOTICE, COPYING), m1-dart/NOTICE-m1n1.txt, m1-dart-survey/NOTICE-m1n1.txt,
m1-dptx/NOTICE, m1-metal/NOTICE, m1-sound/NOTICE, m1-sound/aop/NOTICE,
m1-sound/safetyd/LICENSE, m1-storage/NOTICE, m1-thunderbolt/NOTICE, m1-touchbar/NOTICE,
m1-trackpad-child/multitouch/NOTICE, m1-typec/NOTICE, m1-usb-dwc3/NOTICE. Ten directories
with GPL-derived code have no NOTICE file yet (m1-rust-kext, m1-gpu-rtkit, m1-dcp,
m1-dcp-dart, m1-lkpi-extras, m1-cpufreq, m1-thermal, m1-drm72, m1-native-boot,
m1-avd-capacity); there the SPDX line and notices of each file are the record.
Licence texts: LICENSES/ holds the full text of every licence that files in this repository
are under, and LICENSES/README.md says where each copy came from. LICENSES/third-party/ holds
the licence files of PureDarwin, Finch, m1n1 and Indium with their copyright lines. Upstream
PureDarwin's tree carries PUREDARWIN_LICENSE.txt, APPLE_LICENSE.txt and
APPLE_DRIVER_LICENSE.txt at its top; the vendored Chonkstep copy carries its LICENSE files;
each font recipe installs the font's licence text beside the font.

On an installed system this text is /usr/share/doc/siliconforest/NOTICE. The licence texts
are not installed beside it yet.


PureDarwin
----------
The PureDarwin Project, https://www.puredarwin.org, https://github.com/PureDarwin/PureDarwin
Licence: BSD-2-Clause for PureDarwin's own files ("Copyright (c) 2007-Present The PureDarwin
Project. All rights reserved."; read from PUREDARWIN_LICENSE.txt, copied to
LICENSES/third-party/PureDarwin-LICENSE.txt). APPLE_LICENSE.txt (Apple Public Source License,
Version 2.0, August 6, 2003; read from the file, copied to LICENSES/APSL-2.0.txt) for the
Apple-derived source; each file's own notice. Some of PureDarwin's newer files are
"MPL-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause" as their own notices say.
APPLE_DRIVER_LICENSE.txt, also in upstream's tree, is NOT an open-source licence: it is
Apple's "Binary Driver Software License Agreement", a restrictive licence for Apple driver
binaries (read from the file's head). Which components of PureDarwin it covers has not been
established here; nothing under it may be assumed redistributable.
What we take: all of it. SiliconForest's base tree is PureDarwin's branch upstream-xnu-12377 at
c713d8fb9b048a38e2242d67e29b9957ced8c495 (11 November 2026) with its names changed to
SiliconForest's by tools/sf_rename.py: the XNU build, the kernel extensions and IOKit families,
libSystem, dyld, the Cocotron-derived Foundation and AppKit, CoreFoundation, the window server
and Wayland pieces, the linuxkpi/FreeBSD compatibility layer, the DRM port, the tools
(kc-tools, iig-tools, xnu-loader) and the Nix build. Our changes are patches on that tree.
"PureDarwin" in a copyright line, a licence, a URL or a sentence about upstream is kept.

Apple open-source releases
--------------------------
Apple Inc., https://opensource.apple.com
Licence: Apple Public Source License 2.0, and the other licences of the individual projects
(BSD for parts of XNU and Libc, Apache-2.0 with LLVM exception for dyld's newer parts, …);
not verified beyond each file's own notice.
What we take: through PureDarwin: xnu-12377, IOKit families, libSystem components, dyld,
CoreFoundation, Security, corecrypto (under its own corecrypto licence; not redistributed by
this repository), mDNSResponder, and the other Darwin components PureDarwin builds.
No Apple binary, framework, font, sound or resource is in this repository. (Screenshots of
Apple System 7 that were inside the vendored Chonkstep copy were removed from the tree on
