Source files of Apple's open-source releases appear only as patches against them and as five
copies of IOHIDEventService.cpp under m1-native-input/ with the APSL 2.0 header intact.
The Apple applications run on SiliconForest (Terminal, Activity Monitor) are the owner's
copies and are not part of it.

Asahi Linux and the Linux kernel (through Omacom linux-aurora)
---------------------------------------------------------------
The Asahi Linux contributors and the Linux kernel authors; Omacom's linux-aurora, branch
integration/aurora at 6a08a08e.
Licence: GPL-2.0-only, or GPL-2.0-only OR MIT where a file says so; the Rust GPU driver and
its abstractions GPL-2.0-only OR MIT (as each file's SPDX line says; the per-directory
NOTICE files name the files).
What we take, ported to IOKit (every ported file carries the SPDX line and the original
notices): the PCIe host bridge (pcie-apple.c), the DART IOMMU (apple-dart.c,
io-pgtable-dart.c), RTKit and its mailbox, the AGX GPU driver (drm/asahi, Rust), the DCP
display driver, the SPI HID transport (keyboard, trackpad, Touch Bar digitiser), the Touch
Bar display, the audio drivers (MCA, tas2770, cs42l83, the AOP microphones), the AVD video
decoder, cpufreq and PMGR power states, SMC and its children (RTC, power, reboot), the NVMe
ANS2 glue, the Type-C/ATC PHY, DWC3 and Thunderbolt work in progress, the thermal sensors.
Some Thunderbolt and USB4 family files are taken unchanged (hash-recorded in
integrations/siliconforest/m1-thunderbolt/upstream/).

